  "notes": "Arithmetic mean of dataset-wise Spearman correlations, separately for each trait and method. Every dataset within a trait has equal weight. No averaging across traits, no pooling of contexts, and no sample-size weighting. No interval for the mean is estimated. The constituent context-bootstrap intervals are retained for provenance and are not averaged or plotted. Held-out trait-eliciting evaluation datasets from the R2FAIR P-A extension. Evil and sycophancy use mean graded trait scores; hallucination uses fabrication rates on NQ-Open and SimpleQA. Includes human, automated and model-written evaluations; this is not an exclusively natural-data category. Some evil datasets have little behavioral variation. The same ADD/union map recipe and training-frozen layers as the synthetic and WildChat comparisons are retained. No new model runs or fits. Means describe this fixed dataset roster; no significance claim is made.",
